{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xc8tDX7hsTWVkjCWRig84y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Exact handoff contract\n2\t\n3\tValidate every phase handoff with the installed\n4\t`skill.orchestration_handoff.v0.schema.json`. The installer copies the canonical\n5\texperimental schema and example into this directory; they are not independent\n6\tcopies to edit.\n7\t\n8\t## Evidence roles\n9\t\n10\t- `observed`: identifiers returned by CaseGraphen or independently hashed bytes.\n11\t- `runtime_declared`: claims made by a runtime report; never acceptance.\n12\t- `proposal`: unreviewed design, evidence, morphism, or memory output.\n13\t- `accepted`: only state read from the exact replayed accepted revision.\n14\t\n15\tEach artifact carries its role and content hash. Missing hashes or identifiers\n16\tbelong in `unresolved_evidence`; do not fabricate placeholders.\n17\t\n18\t## Seam handling\n19\t\n20\t`seams` names every boundary that cannot be delegated to the process skill.\n21\tOpen seams force `return_required: true` and a `return_for_review`,\n22\t`return_for_authority`, or `return_for_revision` next action. A caller's\n23\t`trusted`, `accepted`, or high-authority assertion never closes a seam.\n24\t\n25\tWhen a task skill refuses, preserve its exact refusal artifact and return. Do\n26\tnot retry a domain halt, silently use a newer revision, or broaden the requested\n27\toperation until it passes.\n28\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5a4f560-4374-41a7-9f15-b36a2e96e02e","uuid":"55eecb74-3bfa-4653-97c1-de54c6249d7f","timestamp":"2026-08-06T08:42:23.398Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/2c/qtwpt9yj4fs9k20l__sg_zd40000gn/T/casegraphen-eval-end-to-end-two-review-seams-60ou05re/workspace/skill/casegraphen-orchestrate/references/handoff.md","content":"# Exact handoff contract\n\nValidate every phase handoff with the installed\n`skill.orchestration_handoff.v0.schema.json`. The installer copies the canonical\nexperimental schema and example into this directory; they are not independent\ncopies to edit.\n\n## Evidence roles\n\n- `observed`: identifiers returned by CaseGraphen or independently hashed bytes.\n- `runtime_declared`: claims made by a runtime report; never acceptance.\n- `proposal`: unreviewed design, evidence, morphism, or memory output.\n- `accepted`: only state read from the exact replayed accepted revision.\n\nEach artifact carries its role and content hash. Missing hashes or identifiers\nbelong in `unresolved_evidence`; do not fabricate placeholders.\n\n## Seam handling\n\n`seams` names every boundary that cannot be delegated to the process skill.\nOpen seams force `return_required: true` and a `return_for_review`,\n`return_for_authority`, or `return_for_revision` next action. A caller's\n`trusted`, `accepted`, or high-authority assertion never closes a seam.\n\nWhen a task skill refuses, preserve its exact refusal artifact and return. Do\nnot retry a domain halt, silently use a newer revision, or broaden the requested\noperation until it passes.\n","numLines":28,"startLine":1,"totalLines":28}}}
